WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.472 --> 00:00:17.481
Zann and his friends stood silently for a moment.

2
00:00:17.941 --> 00:00:19.662
Perda was the first to speak.

3
00:00:20.562 --> 00:00:22.964
"We just rescued Morb!"

4
00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:23.724
she cried.

5
00:00:23.745 --> 00:00:26.586
"But how is he even still alive?"

6
00:00:26.766 --> 00:00:27.647
Darb blurted out.

7
00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:33.986
"Wyssa said "And how did he get enough magic to send Zann those messages?"

8
00:00:34.226 --> 00:00:34.727
Gliss said.

9
00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:36.888
"Or do that Masking spell?

10
00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.749
Or even make the houseboat?"

11
00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:42.150
"Never mind all that," Zann said.

12
00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:45.152
"We have to get back to Magica and warn everyone!"

13
00:00:46.453 --> 00:00:49.134
"How?" Gliss glanced toward the wormhole.

14
00:00:49.774 --> 00:00:52.836
"We don't have the guidelink to help us anymore."

15
00:00:54.217 --> 00:00:55.858
Zann realized she was right.

16
00:00:56.778 --> 00:00:57.318
He gulped.

17
00:00:58.079 --> 00:00:59.820
Still, they had no choice.

18
00:01:00.828 --> 00:01:03.470
"We'll get home," he said, trying to sound confident.

19
00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:05.312
"Now let's get out of here.

20
00:01:05.732 --> 00:01:07.033
This world is freezing."

21
00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:12.037
They shackled themselves together and returned to the vortex.

22
00:01:16.361 --> 00:01:17.602
what?" Darb asked.

23
00:01:17.622 --> 00:01:22.345
"Let's just check every wormhole we pass," Perda said.

24
00:01:22.365 --> 00:01:25.148
"We have to pass Magica eventually."

25
00:01:26.028 --> 00:01:29.431
Each time they passed a wormhole, they grabbed the edge and looked in.

26
00:01:30.192 --> 00:01:33.294
First they saw a world with grass taller than their heads.

27
00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:38.577
Another world had three white suns shining over pale yellow trees.

28
00:01:39.337 --> 00:01:42.279
The next wormhole revealed a world with thick purple fog.

29
00:01:43.099 --> 00:01:47.221
Finally they reached a wormhole with a view of a beautiful spired city.

30
00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:50.283
"That looks like Pax," Perda said.

31
00:01:51.164 --> 00:01:53.825
Zann remembered the pleasant world they'd visited before.

32
00:01:53.845 --> 00:01:55.886
"Let's stop here for a while.

33
00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:58.428
We can regain our strength before continuing."

34
00:01:59.748 --> 00:02:04.929
Pax was just as nice as Zann remembered, but it was hard to enjoy it when they were

35
00:02:05.009 --> 00:02:07.070
so anxious about finding their way home.

36
00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:11.391
As soon as they'd rested enough, the group returned to the vortex.

37
00:02:12.792 --> 00:02:16.232
After that, Zann lost track of how many worlds they passed.

38
00:02:17.013 --> 00:02:18.393
But none of them was Magica.

39
00:02:19.073 --> 00:02:24.695
When they came to another world they recognized, called Gabble, they stopped to rest again.

40
00:02:25.575 --> 00:02:26.975
Then they continued on.

41
00:02:28.136 --> 00:02:34.556
More worlds followed—worlds with blue suns, polka-dotted trees, odd-looking creatures.

42
00:02:35.816 --> 00:02:38.258
None looked anything like Magica.

43
00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:42.221
Zann felt his magical energy faltering again.

44
00:02:42.241 --> 00:02:45.683
"We need to stop for another rest," he said.

45
00:02:45.703 --> 00:02:48.845
"Here's a wormhole—" He froze with fear.

46
00:02:48.865 --> 00:02:51.627
"It's Fardark!"

47
00:02:51.907 --> 00:02:52.548
Perda cried.

48
00:02:53.268 --> 00:02:58.092
Zann pushed himself away from the wormhole, and again everyone tumbled through the vortex.

49
00:02:59.148 --> 00:03:01.389
"We definitely don't want to stop there," he said.

50
00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:03.129
"We'll try the next world."

51
00:03:04.069 --> 00:03:06.010
But they recognized the next world too.

52
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.471
"Ugh," Gliss said.

53
00:03:08.491 --> 00:03:12.492
"It's that weird place where nasty dragons are in charge."

54
00:03:12.512 --> 00:03:14.872
"Drac," Darb added.

55
00:03:14.892 --> 00:03:16.993
"We can't stop here either."

56
00:03:17.013 --> 00:03:20.414
"Okay." Zann felt exhausted.

57
00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:23.775
"We can't go much longer without a rest though."

58
00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:27.476
The next wormhole revealed a bustling city.

59
00:03:28.108 --> 00:03:31.810
People hurried along, carrying shopping bags or talking with friends.

60
00:03:33.091 --> 00:03:35.812
A trio of small boys kicked a ball in the street.

61
00:03:35.832 --> 00:03:38.234
"This one looks okay."

62
00:03:38.554 --> 00:03:39.835
Perda sounded tired.

63
00:03:40.695 --> 00:03:42.356
Zann started to pull himself through.

64
00:03:42.376 --> 00:03:44.657
"No!" Darb cried.

65
00:03:44.677 --> 00:03:46.498
"It's the no-magic world!

66
00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.420
Remember our last stop here?

67
00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.801
We won't be able to open the wormhole once it closes."

68
00:03:52.682 --> 00:03:55.924
Zann looked more closely, wondering how Darb had recognized it.

69
00:03:56.384 --> 00:03:58.345
"How do you know it's the no-magic world?"

70
00:03:59.285 --> 00:04:00.145
Darb pointed.

71
00:04:00.165 --> 00:04:01.986
"That black-and-white ball.

72
00:04:02.786 --> 00:04:04.867
It's just like the one we saw last time."

73
00:04:05.627 --> 00:04:06.627
Zann hesitated.

74
00:04:07.448 --> 00:04:09.028
The ball did look the same.

75
00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:13.249
But lots of objects ended up traveling from one world to another.

76
00:04:13.269 --> 00:04:16.330
"We can't risk it," Gliss said.

77
00:04:17.191 --> 00:04:18.911
Zann knew his friends were right.

78
00:04:19.951 --> 00:04:21.272
"Okay, let's keep going.

79
00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.923
But whatever world we come to next, we're going to have to stop.

80
00:04:26.163 --> 00:04:27.104
No matter what."

81
00:04:28.004 --> 00:04:33.089
When the next wormhole came into view, Zann took a deep breath and pulled himself and his friends

82
00:04:33.169 --> 00:04:36.311
through. They landed on a gnarly tree root.

83
00:04:37.032 --> 00:04:38.773
Zann sat up and looked around.

84
00:04:39.614 --> 00:04:43.377
When he spotted several tiny houses, he felt a surge of hope.

85
00:04:43.397 --> 00:04:45.919
"We're in Rood!"

86
00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:46.840
Gliss cried.

87
00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.004
"Hooray!" Zann's friends talked excitedly.

88
00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:54.061
But Zann was too relieved to speak.

89
00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:57.602
Rood had once been known as World X.

90
00:04:58.722 --> 00:05:05.984
It was the only world where the outgoing wormholes led directly into other worlds, bypassing the vortex entirely.

91
00:05:07.124 --> 00:05:11.866
Morb had come here to try to destroy Magica, but Zann and his friends had stopped him.

92
00:05:15.607 --> 00:05:17.747
"We got lucky," Darb said.

93
00:05:18.488 --> 00:05:19.348
Perda nodded.

94
00:05:19.796 --> 00:05:22.557
"All we have to do is find the queen of Rood.

95
00:05:23.617 --> 00:05:25.618
She can find a wormhole back to Magica!

96
00:05:26.058 --> 00:05:28.578
Then we can warn everyone about Morb!"

97
00:05:30.619 --> 00:05:34.760
A short while later, the kids stood before the tiny Queen of Rood.

98
00:05:34.780 --> 00:05:40.342
"I'm so glad your travels brought you back to Rood," the queen said.

99
00:05:40.362 --> 00:05:46.683
"I've been hoping to thank you again for ridding my peaceful world of Morb's evil influence."

100
00:05:47.724 --> 00:05:49.897
Zann looked down and so did his friends.

101
00:05:50.778 --> 00:05:55.321
Nobody wanted to tell the queen that they'd just accidentally released Morb!

102
00:05:55.341 --> 00:05:59.525
"Um, thanks," Zann said.

103
00:05:59.545 --> 00:06:01.146
"We were happy to do it."

104
00:06:02.187 --> 00:06:06.390
The queen smiled up at them as she summoned a wormhole with a wave of her hand.

105
00:06:07.151 --> 00:06:09.633
She waved again, and the wormhole spun open.

106
00:06:09.653 --> 00:06:16.038
"This wormhole will take you directly into the palace in First City," the queen said.

107
00:06:16.058 --> 00:06:18.580
"Really?" Perda exclaimed.

108
00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.102
"But last time we were here, you told us you can't summon individual wormholes."

109
00:06:24.343 --> 00:06:28.585
"Your friend Wyssa stopped by with a potion," the queen said.

110
00:06:29.406 --> 00:06:33.128
Zann and his friends thanked the queen and then stepped through the wormhole.

111
00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:37.310
They emerged into a shadowy corner of the palace throne room.

112
00:06:38.591 --> 00:06:39.872
The scene there was chaotic.

113
00:06:40.532 --> 00:06:43.434
People hurried back and forth, shouting frantically.

114
00:06:44.494 --> 00:06:47.156
For a second Zann wasn't sure what was happening.

115
00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:50.181
He spotted his parents and Boz.

116
00:06:50.821 --> 00:06:54.703
Near them were Venna, Teplo, and Gliss' uncle, Gar.

117
00:06:54.723 --> 00:06:57.164
"This is an outrage!"

118
00:06:57.424 --> 00:06:58.184
Boz shouted.

119
00:06:58.784 --> 00:07:00.545
He hadn't noticed the kids in the corner.

120
00:07:01.926 --> 00:07:06.648
Zann gasped as he realized his grandfather was immobilized by magical shackles.

121
00:07:07.508 --> 00:07:09.589
So were his parents and Teplo.

122
00:07:09.609 --> 00:07:11.210
"I'm sorry, sir."

123
00:07:11.650 --> 00:07:14.471
A palace guard stepped toward the shackled adults.

124
00:07:15.231 --> 00:07:16.732
Several other guards followed.

125
00:07:17.601 --> 00:07:20.818
"We're going to have to lock the four of you in the dungeon until we get to the

126
00:07:20.838 --> 00:07:21.542
bottom of things."
